---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import KeybindingTable from '../../components/KeybindingTable.astro';
---

<Docs title="GitHub Workflows" description="Browse and dispatch GitHub Actions workflows from the grüt terminal UI.">
  <h1>GitHub Workflows</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The Workflows tab lists all configured GitHub Actions workflows for your
    repository and lets you trigger workflow dispatch events with custom
    parameters.
  </p>

  <h2>Key Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Workflow list</strong> — All workflows defined in <code>.github/workflows/</code></li>
    <li><strong>Dispatch trigger</strong> — Trigger <code>workflow_dispatch</code> workflows with input parameters directly from the TUI</li>
    <li><strong>Run history</strong> — See recent runs for each workflow</li>
    <li><strong>Preview integration</strong> — Select a workflow to see its definition and recent run status</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keybindings</h2>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: 'Enter', action: 'View workflow details and recent runs' },
    { key: 'D', action: 'Dispatch workflow (if workflow_dispatch enabled)' },
    { key: 'o', action: 'Open workflow in browser' },
    { key: 'y', action: 'Copy workflow URL to clipboard' },
  ]} />

  <h2>Context Awareness</h2>
  <p>
    When you select a workflow, the preview panel shows the workflow YAML
    definition alongside its recent run history. Dispatching a workflow
    prompts you for the ref, then for each declared input in turn: choice and
    boolean inputs are presented as a picker of their valid values (preselected
    on the workflow's default), while free-form inputs offer a text field
    pre-filled with the default so you can accept it or enter a custom value.
  </p>
</Docs>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
